Both are on the path verify-claims runs Python through, and both fail in
the direction that LOSES findings — for a security tool the expensive
error, because a suppressed flow is indistinguishable from a clean repo.

1. SANITIZER GATE PARITY (INV-finoh, second site). propagate_taint_ddg
kept a private copy of sanitizer registration that matched on bare short
name with no is_resolved, call_construct or ambiguous_names filter. Since
a barrier PRUNES the walk, that copy did not merely over-register — an
unrelated unresolved `x.encrypt()` bound Fernet.encrypt and deleted a
real flow. INV-finoh's own root_cause and fix text named TWO sites, "the
helper and its DDG mirror"; the fix landed at the helper, and the closure
evidence was gathered on propagate_taint_structural, which is not the
function Python routes through. Now routed through the shared
_register_sanitizer_callers so the two cannot drift again.

Repro, in the tests: identical 4-node graph, one unresolved bare method
call added on an INTERMEDIATE hop (a collision on the source function
does not reproduce it — the seed is exempt from the barrier check by
design). structural=1 ddg=1 clean; structural=1 ddg=0 poisoned.

2. SINK UNDER-REPORT. sink_callers was a dict keyed on the CALLING
symbol, populated by assignment, so a function calling two different
sinks reported only the last edge encountered. Present in BOTH passes.
Now a list per caller, consumed through a shared _iter_sink_sites so the
loop bodies are untouched and the two passes share one implementation.

MEASURED on the 9-repo cohort, instrument asserted in both directions
before measuring (OK on this branch, BAD:sanitizer_gate_unfixed,
sink_overwrite_structural,sink_overwrite_ddg against dev):

    flows 149 -> 193   added=47  removed=3
    caddy 34 -> 68 (printEnvironment calls both Printf and Println;
    only one was reported), kserve 13 -> 18, pretix 84 -> 88,
    alertmanager 14 -> 15

    ONE CLAIM VERDICT CHANGED: pretix/host-secret-no-network
    confirmed -> violated. A security claim was being reported as
    SATISFIED while it was violated; the under-report hid it.

The 3 "removed" in pretix are NOT removals. pretix's
untrusted-input-no-database verdict sits at exactly 100 evidence rows in
both arms — an output cap over ~741 flows — so adding findings displaces
which 100 are shown. Neither fix can remove a flow: both strictly add
sink sites and strictly remove phantom barriers.

Tests: 1827 passed, 100% coverage on changed files. Positive control
asserted first in both new test classes, so the failures they guard
against cannot pass vacuously.

